  "releaseNotes": "DI019 no longer treats a custom wrapper's `ServiceProvider` property as the root provider; only the singleton's own or inherited provider properties, known host properties, and real scope providers qualify. | DI001 treats a scope wrapped in a directly returned object as caller-owned, while still reporting a wrapper stored locally without disposal. | The pinned scan corpus is now 14 public repositories and 471 findings, adding `jasontaylordev/CleanArchitecture` and `elsa-workflows/elsa-core`.",
